# Cpredict reverse-tunnel package for @@PUBLIC_HOST@@

This generated package exposes the local Cpredict service without running Docker on the cloud host:

```text
colleague -> HTTPS/Basic Auth -> cloud Nginx -> 127.0.0.1:@@REMOTE_PORT@@
          -> restricted SSH reverse tunnel -> local 127.0.0.1:@@LOCAL_PORT@@
```

The package is bound to SSH endpoint `@@SSH_HOST@@:@@SSH_PORT@@` and Ed25519 host-key fingerprint
`@@HOST_KEY_SHA256@@`. Verify `SHA256SUMS` before installation. Never copy the generated private key to
the cloud host.

## Ordered installation

### Recommended two-command path

After generating this package, the Mac helper can prepare the local key/launchd service, upload the
package with pinned host-key checking, run the interactive cloud installer, start the tunnel, and run
both verification commands:

```bash
bash macos/cpredict-tunnel deploy-cloud \
  --admin-user ubuntu \
  --admin-key /absolute/path/to/cloud-admin-key \
  --basic-auth-user colleague \
  --install-autossh \
  --disable-default-site
```

The admin key may be passphrase protected. Sudo and the new Basic Auth password can prompt in the same
terminal; passwords are never command arguments. If upload, installation or verification fails, the
command prints and retains the exact remote `/tmp/cpredict-reverse-tunnel.*` directory for diagnosis.
On success it removes that temporary upload.

### Manual/recovery path

1. On the Mac, keep the local Compose stack ready on `127.0.0.1:@@LOCAL_PORT@@`, then prepare the key
   without starting the tunnel:

   ```bash
   bash macos/cpredict-tunnel install --install-autossh --defer-start
   ```

2. Copy only `~/.cpredict/reverse-tunnel/id_ed25519.pub` and this generated package to the cloud host.

3. On a clean Ubuntu 24.04 cloud host, run:

   ```bash
   sudo bash cloud/cpredict-tunnel-cloud install \
     --public-key-file ./id_ed25519.pub \
     --basic-auth-user colleague \
     --disable-default-site
   ```

   The password prompt comes from `htpasswd`; do not place the password on the command line. Use
   `--reuse-htpasswd` only after reviewing an existing `/etc/nginx/cpredict.htpasswd`.

4. Back on the Mac, start the launch agent and verify both sides:

   ```bash
   ~/.cpredict/reverse-tunnel/cpredict-tunnel restart
   ~/.cpredict/reverse-tunnel/cpredict-tunnel verify
   sudo cpredict-tunnel-cloud verify
   ```

The cloud `verify` command is the acceptance point that proves the live loopback listener and the local
`/readyz` response. The Mac must remain plugged in; the worker uses `caffeinate -s` while it is running,
and launchd restarts it after network loss or process exit.

## Operations

Both commands support `status`, `verify`, `logs`, `restart`, and `uninstall`. The Mac uninstall retains
the dedicated key unless `--delete-key` is explicit. The cloud uninstall removes only package-managed
configuration and the dedicated tunnel user; it intentionally retains Nginx, Certbot and certificates.

Do not expose TCP @@REMOTE_PORT@@ in the cloud security group or firewall. Only 80/443 are public; SSH
must be restricted to the operator and Mac egress source CIDRs. The installer deliberately does not
change provider security groups or UFW because guessing the management CIDR could lock out the host.
